==English==
{{rft}}
===Etymology 1===
Possibly an ellipsis of "Could you come again with what you just said?" "Come again with what you just said."

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb|head=[[come]] [[again]]}}

# {{idiomatic|informal}} Could you repeat that? Repeat that please. {{non-gloss definition|a polite formula used when one has not heard or understood what has been said}}
#* '''1955''', [[w:Rex Stout|Rex Stout]], "When a Man Murders...",<!--... in title--> in [[w:Three Witnesses (book)|''Three Witnesses'']], October 1994 [[w:Bantam Books|Bantam]] edition, ISBN 0553249592, page 120:
#*:"Who says he did?" / "Aubry." / "Yeah? A guy in for murder? '''Come again.'''" / "Glad to. Beebe says so too."

=====Synonyms=====
* [[excuse me]] {{qualifier|especially US}}, [[I beg your pardon]] {{qualifier|formal}}, [[pardon]], [[sorry]], [[what]], [[say again]]

